ghelper-linux (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Headless UI smoke tests build the real application and open the main,
    Settings, Fans and Power, and Hotkeys windows.
  * A GTK critical now fails the test run instead of being ignored.
  * CI runs the UI tests under Xvfb with private session and system buses.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:56:50 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fans and Power: distinct auto-apply labels, Apply Power Limits next to
    the sliders, and sliders that use the spare height.
  * Status text is no longer styled like a link.
  * Hotkeys opens compact with a mapped-keys header and an empty-state hint.
  * The battery limit is labelled separately from live charge, and the
    keyboard colour swatch has a border and a tooltip.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:20:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Installs work from any prefix: the polkit policy follows the install
    prefix, the launcher records the rescan helper's directory, and the
    automation unit finds the binary through PATH.
  * --page opens only the requested window, and the asusd banner shows the
    live error instead of the startup message.
  * Settings no longer retries a failed refresh in a tight loop when asusd
    is unavailable.
  * AC/battery automation resumes after the user leaves Smart or Manual
    mode; the tray keeps profile and GPU radios in separate groups.
  * nouveau dGPU temperatures are reported when no amdgpu dGPU is present,
    and --check reports the resolved rescan helper.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:40:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Refresh-rate control stays read-only on desktops other than KDE Plasma
    and says so, instead of failing with a KWin error on GNOME or wlroots.
  * AppStream metadata now links to the project homepage and issue tracker.
  * CI builds a Debian package alongside the RPM.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:20:00 -0500
